senses.gloss:
क्रुश् क्रुश्, cl. 1. P. (rarely A.) क्रोशति,
-ते, चुक्रोश, क्रोक्ष्यति, अक्रुक्षत्,
क्रोष्टुम्, to cry out, shriek, yell, bawl, call out, halloo;
to exclaim; to cry, lament; to weep; to sound, make
a singing noise (as the ear): Caus. क्रोशयति, -यि-
तुम्: Desid. चुक्रुक्षति: Intens. चोक्रुश्यते,
चोक्रुशीति; [cf. Lith. klykiu, ‘to cry;’ kryksztauju;
Hib. cruisigh, ‘music, song;’ Lat. crocis, crocito;
Gr. κρώζω, κράζω, κραγγή; Goth. krukya.]
